Here’s the updated process, please review:

Drivers operating in the Johannesburg, Cape Town, Port Elizabeth and Durban area need to complete a mandatory background check within 48 hours after they are activated. The background check needs to be redone every year. 

h3. Background check process

* Driver will receive an SMS with a link to find the MIE centre
Driver visits a centre and their fingerprints are taken
Fingerprints are submitted to MIE for a background check
Once the results are ready, they will be delivered back to Bolt
If the driver receives a negative result, they will be allowed to continue operating
* If the driver receives a positive or inconclusive result, they will be blocked
** Advise the driver that they should connect with the Department of Justice to initiate the [+expungements+|http://www.justice.gov.za/expungements.html] process
Once their record has been expunged, they should return to the Raspberry MIE offices to have their fingerprints retaken
If they pass, their account will be reactivated

*Note:* Drivers are *not* required to submit MIE documentation in order to be unblocked

h3. Additional information

* Drivers can complete their background checks Monday to Friday between 08:30 and 15:30. Addresses are available on the[ +RaspberryONE webpage+|https://www.raspberryone.co.za/]. 
The check fee applied to every background check is R 200.00 and can only be paid by card.

h3. {color:#36b37e}The driver submits a ticket with the MIE report asking to be unblocked{color}

{color:#36b37e}*Tier 1:*{color}

* {color:#36b37e}Ensure the driver has attached a correct document{color}
** {color:#36b37e}The report is issued by MIE{color}
** {color:#36b37e}The branch is Raspberry{color}
** {color:#36b37e}The report is requested by Bolt{color}
** {color:#36b37e}The driver details (under {color}{color:#36b37e}_Candidate_{color}{color:#36b37e}) match with the ones on their Admin profile{color}
* {color:#36b37e}Check if the result is negative{color}
** {color:#36b37e}If it is positive or inconclusive, follow the relevant steps mentioned above (under the {color}{color:#36b37e}*Background check*{color}{color:#36b37e} section){color}
* {color:#36b37e}Escalate the ticket to Tier 2{color}

{color:#36b37e}*Tier 2:*{color}

* {color:#36b37e}Escalate the ticket to OPS via the cs-ops-escalations Slack channel{color}
* {color:#36b37e}Advise the driver that their request has been forwarded to the relevant team.{color}

Looking forward to your reply,

