Hi Fabian, many thanks for this broader context, this is very helpful.

With phase 1 of this project, we are mostly in the clear from privacy side, since (a) we won’t collect any personal data or (b) disclose any PII.  No consent is required here. If this is agreed upon with our partners, then their contact details can be displayed on this landing page. One recommendation here is to ensure that the e-mail addresses of our fleet partners available on the website won’t be personally identifiable and be rather generic such as c[ontact@domain.com|mailto:contact@domain.com] so it wouldn’t fall under the scope of data protection legislation.

However, when you will be considering moving things forward with collecting personal data, then please keep our privacy team in the loop as following actions will be required:

* InfoSec review of the landing page and data collection process;
* drafting and putting in place privacy policy for the end-users;
* if data collection would involve tracking- putting in place cookie consent banner + cookie policy;
* reviewing if any contractual provision with our fleet owners will be required.

Best,

Adriana

