Hi [~accountid:5bb34560eec89a2b8534aaff] 
I see that the main changes that the Partner has made can be summarised as follows: 
- Partner wants a penalty of 100% of the Goods price if Bolt is late to send the agency report or if there’re any mistakes therein - this is against Bolt’s interests. I know that sometimes we might have minor mistakes, and it not be in our interests to pay penalties; 
- Partner wants Bolt to transfer all the money received from clients (without deduction of the Agency fee) - that creates a risk for Bolt that the Partner will receive all funds from us and than will refuse to pay the Agency fee; 
- Partner wants Bolt to issue not only Agency report, but also invoices - I doubt that Commerce can build a separate process especially for this Partner; 
- Partner wants Bolt to pay interest of 2x NBU for each day of delay - this is against Bolt’s interests; 
- Partner wants to get access to our bank account to write off funds from our bank account without our consent in case of any alleged debt - this is unreasonable and we can’t accept it; 
- Partner insists that Bolt shall not have the right to charge Marketplace Fees without the Partner’s consent in writing - this creates a risk that Bolt will be unable to charge Marketplace Fees at all; 
- Partner has crossed fully the sections regarding the Tablet and the Photos - not sure what it means. 

Overall, how big is this partner to negotiate this fees? If they’re a key partner, let’s discuss with Ivan whether we can make any concessions. Please note that all of the amendments are against Bolt’s interests.

